1) triangulations. make them robust, with incircle tests and refinement

2) sphere groups, possibly with orbifold

3) marked triangulations

4) rational maps, recorded by critical points and values (rather than coefficients), and normalization. (in degree 1, misses 3 params; in degree 2, misses 1 param. in degree >=3, probably ok).
- conversion to classical format
- equations that enforce the points to be consistent
- compute preimages of points in this model, test intersection between curve (arc of great circle) and curve.
